# LEVEL CONSIDERATIONS
  The Sigma rule alone provides low-confidence detection.
  High-confidence detection is achieved through SIEM-side correlation as described in the Correlation Logic section.
  Consequently, the Sigma rule severity is Low while correlated alert severity varies according to the observed scanning pattern.

# IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
  The Sigma rule represents the initial network connection detection layer.
  High-confidence alert generation should be performed through SIEM-side correlation using:
    - SourceIp
    - DestinationIp
    - DestinationPort
  correlation within a 1-minute time window as described in the Correlation Logic section.

